{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["<b>And these are the sons of Shuthelach, etc.</b> The rest of the sons of Shuthelach — their genealogies are named after Shuthelach. And from Eiran a large family went out and is named after him, and the sons of Shuthelach were counted as two families. Go and count and you will find in this passage fifty-seven families, and from the sons of Levi eight — here are sixty-five. And this is what is said: ״כִּי אַתֶּם הַמְעַט״ and so on — the meaning is מְעַט: you are five short of the families of all the peoples, which are seventy. This too I have drawn from the foundation of Rabbi Moshe ha-Darshan, but I needed to subtract from and add to his words."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:12:54.931566540Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}